  "courseSlug": "remix-course",
  "courseTitle": "Remix.js - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "34674772",
      "title": "Understanding Splat Routes",
      "lectureOrder": 53,
      "videoOrder": 48,
      "sourceHash": "acf51619c43718cc4638da09d9e7dce3c5a5d62832ecdabe0e3943b48dc45059",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.19,
          "end": 4.02,
          "en": "Now that we know about resource routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.02,
          "end": 5.61,
          "en": "we are indeed almost done",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.61,
          "end": 7.823,
          "en": "with all the different route features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.823,
          "end": 9.354,
          "en": "There are a lot of features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.354,
          "end": 11.91,
          "en": "but they hopefully all make sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 11.91,
          "end": 14.16,
          "en": "There's just one last feature left",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 14.16,
          "end": 16.05,
          "en": "which I also want to explore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 16.05,
          "end": 18,
          "en": "and that would be splat routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 18,
          "end": 20.22,
          "en": "Now, what's a splat route?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 20.22,
          "end": 23.31,
          "en": "A splat route is a route which you create like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 23.31,
          "end": 27.81,
          "en": "You add a file and you name it dollar sign dot jsx.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 27.81,
          "end": 31.705,
          "en": "So dollar sign without anything after it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 31.705,
          "end": 34.89,
          "en": "We know the dollar sign from Dynamic Routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.89,
          "end": 36.54,
          "en": "but then we had something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 36.54,
          "end": 40.403,
          "en": "after the dollar sign, some placeholder name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.403,
          "end": 43.39,
          "en": "Now it's just dollar sign Jsx",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.28,
          "end": 46.95,
          "en": "and Remix will activate that route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.95,
          "end": 50.37,
          "en": "and load whatever we're going to write in this file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.37,
          "end": 52.92,
          "en": "whenever no other route matches.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 52.92,
          "end": 56.28,
          "en": "And then the special thing is that it will give us access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.28,
          "end": 60.03,
          "en": "to all the path segments that were entered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.03,
          "end": 61.77,
          "en": "Now this might sound a bit strange",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 61.77,
          "end": 65.283,
          "en": "and abstract and therefore all simply show you how it works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.18,
          "end": 70.292,
          "en": "We can again, export a loader here, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.292,
          "end": 73.44,
          "en": "Now that loader receives a data object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.44,
          "end": 76.11,
          "en": "which has a param's object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.11,
          "end": 78.81,
          "en": "So I'm using object destructuring here to get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.81,
          "end": 81.27,
          "en": "to the params object, which is stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.27,
          "end": 84.3,
          "en": "under a param's property in that overall object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 84.3,
          "end": 86.82,
          "en": "which I receive as an argument here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 86.82,
          "end": 89.34,
          "en": "I talked about this params object already",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.34,
          "end": 91.233,
          "en": "in the Remix Essentials section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 92.43,
          "end": 95.22,
          "en": "Now let me console lock the params object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 95.22,
          "end": 98.253,
          "en": "so that you see what's inside of it, how it looks like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.45,
          "end": 101.46000000000001,
          "en": "And I'll then simply return nullll",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 101.46000000000001,
          "end": 103.38300000000001,
          "en": "because we must return something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.25,
          "end": 108.24000000000001,
          "en": "And now let's say that we enter some path like",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 108.24000000000001,
          "end": 110.10300000000001,
          "en": "A B C slash D.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 110.97,
          "end": 114.47999999999999,
          "en": "Now I get null here because that's what I'm returning.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 114.47999999999999,
          "end": 115.74000000000001,
          "en": "But the interesting part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 115.74000000000001,
          "end": 118.874,
          "en": "is what's being logged here in the console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 118.874,
          "end": 122.673,
          "en": "There you can see that this is being logged.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 123.6,
          "end": 125.6,
          "en": "This is this console log statement here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.8,
          "end": 131.76,
          "en": "So what we're getting here as params is an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 131.76,
          "end": 135.09,
          "en": "which has an asterisk key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 135.09,
          "end": 138.363,
          "en": "and then the path that was entered as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139.95,
          "end": 142.82999999999998,
          "en": "So whatever was entered here as a path is the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 142.82999999999998,
          "end": 145.5,
          "en": "for this special asterisk key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 145.5,
          "end": 148.86,
          "en": "And that's the special thing about these splat routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 148.86,
          "end": 152.94,
          "en": "They don't just activate whenever no other route matches",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.94,
          "end": 156.953,
          "en": "but they then also contain all path segments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 156.953,
          "end": 160.65,
          "en": "in their params under this special asterisk key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 160.65,
          "end": 161.733,
          "en": "as you can see here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 162.57,
          "end": 166.653,
          "en": "Now, why would such splat routes possibly be useful?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.82,
          "end": 170.13,
          "en": "Well, let's say that we had an older version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.13,
          "end": 173.67000000000002,
          "en": "of the website where we loaded the expenses page not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.67000000000002,
          "end": 177.12,
          "en": "for slash expenses, but for slash x.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 177.12,
          "end": 179.34,
          "en": "At the moment, this does not work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 179.34,
          "end": 180.963,
          "en": "because this is not supported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 181.86,
          "end": 185.04,
          "en": "Well that's exactly where a splat route could help us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.04,
          "end": 188.04,
          "en": "We could use it to set up some redirects here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 188.04,
          "end": 189.87,
          "en": "We could check if",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 189.87,
          "end": 193.29,
          "en": "params and then use this special asterisk key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 193.29,
          "end": 195.9,
          "en": "is maybe equal to just X.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 195.9,
          "end": 197.46,
          "en": "And in that case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 197.46,
          "end": 202.46,
          "en": "we return our redirect using this redirect function provided",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 202.53,
          "end": 207.53,
          "en": "by Remix run, which simply generates a redirect request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 207.54,
          "end": 209.913,
          "en": "and we redirect to slash expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 211.29,
          "end": 212.22,
          "en": "That would be one way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 212.22,
          "end": 215.25,
          "en": "of utilizing such a splat route to implement logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 215.25,
          "end": 216.273,
          "en": "for redirecting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 217.47,
          "end": 219.87,
          "en": "So if that's the case, and we then reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 219.87,
          "end": 221.883,
          "en": "you see for slash x,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 222.93,
          "end": 225.21,
          "en": "I'm now redirected to slash expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 225.21,
          "end": 226.923,
          "en": "because of this splat route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 227.85,
          "end": 230.04,
          "en": "We could implement such redirection patterns",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 230.04,
          "end": 232.07999999999998,
          "en": "all the four more complex paths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 232.07999999999998,
          "end": 234.54,
          "en": "since we get all path segments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 234.54,
          "end": 236.973,
          "en": "under this special asterisk key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 238.07999999999998,
          "end": 240.72,
          "en": "And of course we could say that if we don't redirect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 240.72,
          "end": 242.67,
          "en": "then I don't wanna return null",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 242.67,
          "end": 245.76,
          "en": "but I maybe wanna throw a response, which we can do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 245.76,
          "end": 249.57,
          "en": "by instantiating the default response class here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 249.57,
          "end": 251.793,
          "en": "which is provided by Node.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 252.66,
          "end": 256.11,
          "en": "And we for example, give it a text of not found",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 256.11,
          "end": 257.49,
          "en": "and then a second argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 257.49,
          "end": 260.4,
          "en": "where we set the status code to 4 0 4.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 260.4,
          "end": 262.5,
          "en": "Now this here is not a Remix feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 262.5,
          "end": 266.1,
          "en": "This is the standard response constructor function step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 266.1,
          "end": 270.27,
          "en": "the standard response class where the first argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 270.27,
          "end": 272.61,
          "en": "is the body that will be passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 272.61,
          "end": 274.65,
          "en": "to the response that's being generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 274.65,
          "end": 276.65999999999997,
          "en": "in this case, just some text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 276.65999999999997,
          "end": 278.52,
          "en": "And the second argument can be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 278.52,
          "end": 280.2,
          "en": "for configuring the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 280.2,
          "end": 283.5,
          "en": "For example, it's headers or it's status code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 283.5,
          "end": 284.58,
          "en": "And when using Remix,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 284.58,
          "end": 286.983,
          "en": "we can throw such responses as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 288.06,
          "end": 291.6,
          "en": "If I do that and I enter anything else like A B C",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 291.6,
          "end": 294.273,
          "en": "then I get this not found response, therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 295.56,
          "end": 299.49,
          "en": "So that's what we could do with splat routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 299.49,
          "end": 302.31,
          "en": "You won't need them in all your applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 302.31,
          "end": 303.84,
          "en": "and in all scenarios",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 303.84,
          "end": 307.71,
          "en": "but they can sometimes be useful and you can also nest them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 307.71,
          "end": 312.06,
          "en": "We could add it here in the expenses folder if we wanted to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 312.06,
          "end": 315.18,
          "en": "and then it would catch all requests that are not matched",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 315.18,
          "end": 317.4,
          "en": "by the other routes in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 317.4,
          "end": 320.28,
          "en": "So that's what you can do with splat routes here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 320.28,
          "end": 322.23,
          "en": "I'll keep it on the route level for now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 322.23,
          "end": 324.93,
          "en": "even though we don't need it for this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 324.93,
          "end": 326.25,
          "en": "But as a developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 326.25,
          "end": 328.953,
          "en": "you should definitely know about splat routes.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
